# What the turn dispatch model stands for. .agents/skills/turn-dispatch says how to keep it true:
# its Coverage record maps each model action to the code below.
#
# sync: the commit whose code the model was last confirmed to describe (SLNT-1017's full run).
# Move it only as the skill's step 1 and full run say. 987a04461d is mend#1739's commit on the
# SLNT-895 feature branch rebased on main; its covered files are the ones SLNT-1017's run checked.
# 0e0b2722ca is the SLNT-1113 branch rebased on main: agent-conversation.ts gained newestItems, a
# read of each session's newest item whose turn still runs, for the inbox, and nothing else. It
# claims, binds, completes or cancels no turn, so no action models it; SLNT-895's squash changed no
# covered function. Full run at 0e0b2722ca: every row as expected.
# 764de6838d is the SLNT-1199 branch: agent-conversation.ts gained inboxTurnFacts, two grouped
# reads (whether a session has a turn queued or running, and its newest turn or request time) for
# the inbox, and nothing else. It claims, binds, completes or cancels no turn, so no action models
# it. Full run at 764de6838d: every row as expected.
# 38a41001d0 is the SLNT-1211 branch rebased on main (#1910): agent-conversation.ts gained firstMessages, one read of each
# session's lowest-ordinal turn Mend sent and still in its history (an unnamed session's title, and
# the namer's first prompt), and nothing else. It claims, binds, completes or cancels no turn, so no
# action models it. Full run at 752341b3fe, its commit before the rebase: every row as expected.
# 4c6808f4ff is the SLNT-1230 branch: agent-conversation.ts gained openingMessages, one read of a
# session's first few turns Mend sent and still in its history (the namer reads past a first "hi"),
# and nothing else. It claims, binds, completes or cancels no turn, so no action models it. Full
# run at 4c6808f4ff: every row as expected.
# 792ac83bf1 is the SLNT-1234 branch: when the agent takes a message sent into its running turn,
# Codex's user message carries the steer's id (codex.ts sends it on turn/steer and reports the
# item as steer.taken), protocol-host.ts handles steer.taken, and agent-conversation.ts gained
# markTurnSteerTaken, which stamps a steer row's taken_at. None writes a turn's status or provider
# turn id, nor touches turn/start, turn.started or turn/completed, so no action models it. Full run
# at 792ac83bf1: every row as expected.
# 61bf84dcb8 is the SLNT-1233 branch on main at 665d4b68dd, whose covered files carry nothing since
# 792ac83bf1 but SLNT-1234's squash, which the line before accounted for. agent-conversation.ts
# gained setTurnMemoryLimit, which writes an ended turn's memory_limit (the workspace reached its
# memory limit during it) and nothing else, and toTurn decodes that column. Neither writes a turn's
# status or provider turn id, nor claims, binds, completes or cancels one, so no action models it.
# Full run at 61bf84dcb8: every row as expected.
# cb5993b958 is the same SLNT-1233 commit rebased on main at 6d443dff6, whose two new commits
# changed no covered file: the covered code is 61bf84dcb8's, which the full run above checked.
# 4681d853dc is the SLNT-1237 branch: the model gained the start (Starts, Attach, ATake, WRead,
# WAdmit, WTake, LaunchFails, StopAsk, Settle) and NeverStranded, for waiting turns
# (admitTurnMessage with no process, takeWaitingTurns at attachInternal and in waitForStart,
# endWaitingTurns, queueOpeningTurn, rekeyWaitingTurn) and cancelOpenForTurn's notify. Full run at
# 4681d853dc: every row as expected, counts as ROWS pins.
sync 4681d853dcc5273dbb2aa29b6ac8459f5999d8a6

model TurnDispatch.tla
model MCTurnDispatch.tla
model check.sh

path packages/sessions/src/protocol-host.ts
path packages/db/src/repos/agent-conversation.ts
path packages/agent-protocol/src/codex.ts

# How long check.sh may run on CI's four-core runner before formal.mjs stops it and fails
# naming this model (SLNT-1065, SLNT-1081). With tlx the full bounds took 2.3 minutes on CI (run
# 44103197639) and --quick 3 seconds: about 3.4 minutes on a host 1.5 times slower, and
# budget-full is about twice that. SLNT-1237's start (waiting turns) about doubled the full run
# (53 s to about 100 s locally on 4 workers), so budget-full doubled with it.
budget-quick 5
budget-full 16
